<title>JAPAN: Fujisawa boosts capital of key European unit.</title>
<headline>Fujisawa boosts capital of key European unit.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fujisawa Pharmaceutical Co Ltd said on Monday that it had raised the capital of one of its units, Fujisawa Holland BV, by about 3.2 billion yen in order to expand its business in Europe.</p>
<p>The subsidiary is a wholly owned subsidiary of Fujisawa which functions as a holding company for Fujisawa's other European units, a Fujisawa spokesman said.</p>
<p>He said that move was aimed at expanding sales of its PROGRAF drug and boosting other businesses in Europe.</p>
<p>PROGRAF helps prevent organ rejection in transplant patients.</p>
</text>
